to kick-off the 2019 Karen's Cup we're  here today at the community day with  Scouts BSA which as of two days ago are  now allowing girls to join the scouting  program so we have our very first  all-girls scouting merit badge for chess  [Music]  a group of girls who came out to get  their Scouts merit badge and these are  among the first girls ever to get this  badge it was really exciting I gave a  little presentation about some of the  top tactics from women players in the  world which I thought was a really fun  kickoff for the day and for the Karen's  Cup  so now boys and girls are both in the  program the kickoff was February first  so we saw that this is one of the first  merit badge skill centers available for  girls right after the kickoff so we have  two girls from our troop very excited  and I see there's lots of other girls  from the area that are joining so it's  really exciting to see such interest in  the area another thing that really  excited me was to see the girls helping  each other because that's a lot about  what getting the badge is not just about  becoming a good chess player it's also  about community and making sure that  other people can get the benefits of  chess  [Music]  having the top female players in the  world here in st. Louis is really a  great opportunity for st. Louis area  girls who have joined the scouting  program to be able to to see their idols  and meet some of these amazing chess  players and to learn what it's like to  be a professional female chess player  [Music]
 

